#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hao-embed: give arm64/arm64e-only Mach-O executables an x86_64 slice.

The new slice is hao-stub signed ad hoc with the program's own signing
identifier and entitlements (plus the JIT entitlements hao needs), with the
hardened runtime when the program is a platform or hardened-runtime binary
(dyld then ignores DYLD_* variables for the stub, as for the program). On Intel
the kernel selects it, so the process keeps the program's path, name and
code identity; the stub runs the file's own arm64e slice through libhao.
The original slices are copied byte for byte (tools/hao_fat.py).

  hao-embed [--stub PATH] [--host-test] [--translate] [--x86-cache DIR] -o OUT PROGRAM...   embedded copies
  hao-embed [--stub PATH] [--host-test] [--translate] [--x86-cache DIR] --in-place PROGRAM...
  hao-embed [--stub PATH] [--translate] --stubs DIR --root ROOT [--x86-cache DIR] [--list FILE | --scan]
            [--require REL]... [--require-embedded] [PROGRAM...]
  hao-embed --scan ROOT                                       list arm64-only programs
      signed stubs + DIR/manifest.json for installing into an image whose
      files under ROOT match (tools/hao-image-payload, hao-install.py);
      "required" in the manifest lists the paths hao-install.py must embed
      (--require REL, or every entry with --require-embedded). --scan lists
      every path of a hard-linked program (each gets its own entry, so the
      installer embeds each path even if the image builder broke the link)

--translate: a universal program (x86_64 plus arm64e or arm64) has its own
x86_64 slices dropped and gets the stub instead, exactly as an arm64-only
program does: same identity, entitlements and carried sections, all taken
from the arm slice hao runs (arm64e first). Its manifest entry says
"mode": "translate"; source_sha256 is the original universal file.
Without --translate, files that already have an x86_64 slice are skipped.

--save-skeletons DIR also writes each relinked stub as ld left it, with its program's carried sections
and LC_UUID zeroed (DIR/<program sha256>.skel and .json, the sections' offsets): no bytes of the program,
so it may be distributed. --skeletons DIR fills those from each program instead of running ld and gives
the same stub, so a Mac without Apple's ld for the stub's deployment target can embed (hao-image-payload
writes OUT/embed/skeletons).

The stub's build directory is the directory of --stub (default build/):
relinked stubs use its front/stub.o, libhao.dylib and libhao_identity.dylib, the deployment target
in front/stub.o's LC_BUILD_VERSION (make MACOS_MIN=...; the program's build
version replaces it after the link) and the LC_RPATHs of the --stub binary
itself, so they are linked as the Makefile links hao-stub.
The manifest records each entry's stub hash and the hashes of those inputs,
the stub's LC_UUID and platform, how many libraries it links ("links", "weak_links"), the
dependencies it does not ("not_linked": name and why), whether CoreFoundation
is among its launch images ("corefoundation"), and the x86_64 cache's UUID.

Every stub is linked, after libhao and libhao_identity, against the program's
own dependencies that load natively, in the program's load-command order
(weak ones weak; re-exports and upward ones as plain loads), so the images
dyld has initialised when libSystem starts (libsecinit sets up the app
sandbox then, and grants launchservicesd only if CoreFoundation is among
them) are the native program's. A dependency loads natively when, as
src/runtime.c binds it, it is an install name of the target's x86_64 shared
cache (--x86-cache DIR: the directory of its dyld_shared_cache_x86_64;
default with --stubs the one under --root, else this host's) or a file under
ROOT with an x86_64 slice; an @rpath one resolves through the program's LC_RPATHs (which
every stub carries). Not linked: arm64-only libraries (guest images), missing ones,
lazy loads, and a fat file the program calls with C++ names (the runtime may
run it as guest code, src/runtime.c guest_cxx_library). The stubs link
against install-name-only text stubs (.tbd, the program's own versions),
so no x86_64 library is read at link time.

Every stub has its own LC_UUID: a version 5 UUID (STUB_UUID_NAMESPACE) of the
program's arm slice LC_UUID and of the stub's own sections (their names,
addresses and bytes), so logd and everything else keyed by the main
executable's UUID tell programs apart, and payloads stay reproducible. Files
that are one program natively (hard links, copies with the same LC_UUID)
share it, as their arm64e slices do. A UUID names one image's contents to
its readers: logd saves the format strings of a UUID once (uuidtext) and
resolves every later record of that UUID in the saved copy, so a stub whose
code or strings lie elsewhere (another hao build of the same program) must
not reuse the UUID.

Every stub carries its program's load-time identity by rule: each load
command type of the arm slice is copied, derived or denied as
tools/stub_identity_gate.py's RULES says (with who reads it), and a program
with a type the table does not name, or a refused one, is refused. After the
link, the arm slice's LC_BUILD_VERSION (platform, minos, sdk, tools),
LC_SOURCE_VERSION, LC_RPATHs (after the stub's own) and LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT
are written into the stub's header, with LC_MAIN's stacksize, the MH flags
the kernel reads and libSystem's link versions (at its place in the
program's dependency order); __PAGEZERO's size is the program's; the
signature gets the program's CS kill/hard/enforcement flags. dyld takes the
process's platform from the main executable (a Mac Catalyst program may load
/System/iOSSupport images that a macOS process may not; libhao and
libhao_identity are macOS-only images, which dyld loads into a Catalyst
process), dyld_get_program_sdk_version, NSVersionOfLinkTimeLibrary and the
frameworks' linked-on-or-after checks read it, and dyld expands @rpath for
native dlopens through the main executable's rpaths. An arm slice with no
build version or more than one (zippered) is refused.
tools/stub_identity_gate.py checks embedded files or a --stubs payload
against the rules (hao-image-payload runs it on every payload).

The stub carries copies of the sections native code reads from the main
executable (CARRY below: Info.plist, launchd/xpc sections, marker segments
such as __SLSERVER and __RESTRICT).

The stub's signature does not cover the arm slice, so every stub names the
slice it was made for: __TEXT,__hao_slice holds the hash type and cdhash of
the arm slice's CodeDirectory (slice_record; src/libval.c hao_libval_bound
refuses to load any other slice under that stub). The arm slice's signature
must therefore be valid as hao checks it (tools/hao_codesig.py check:
structure and page hashes); a program whose arm slice is unsigned or does not
verify is refused.

A bundle's main executable (X.app/Contents/MacOS/X, .appex, .xpc, ...) is
signed with its bundle: its CodeDirectory binds Contents/Info.plist (special
slot -1) and _CodeSignature/CodeResources (slot -3), which is where libsecinit
(app sandbox containers), LaunchServices, TCC and SecCode* read the bundle
identifier and resource seal. codesign signs the stub as a bare file, so the
stub's slots -1 and -3 are then set to what the arm slice binds (each checked
against the bundle's file, or for slot -1 a tool's carried __info_plist), and
cleared where it binds nothing (bound_data). The bundle's files are only read.
The manifest's "bound" list names each bound file (relative to --root) and its
SHA-256; hao-install.py embeds the stub only if the target's file matches.

--in-place keeps the file's inode: every hard link to it is embedded too.
A symlink is refused (embed the file it names).
--host-test keeps only public entitlements and adds an rpath to that build
directory, so a stub run on the development host finds its libhao.dylib.

Files that are not LC_MAIN executables are skipped, and so is a PROGRAM
whose real path was already given (a repeated path or a symlink alias).
Exit status 1 if any file failed.
"""
import argparse
import hashlib
import json
import os
import plistlib
import shutil
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import uuid

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
import hao_codesig  # noqa: E402
import hao_fat  # noqa: E402
import stub_identity_gate as identity_rules  # noqa: E402

DEFAULT_STUB = os.path.join(HERE, "..", "build", "hao-stub")
LC_BUILD_VERSION, LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX = 0x32, 0x24
JIT_ENTITLEMENTS = {
    "com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit": True,
    "com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation": True,
}
MH_EXECUTE = 2
CPU_SUBTYPE_ARM64E = 2
# What native code reads from the main executable (whose Mach-O header is
# the stub's), by section name through libmacho (getsectbyname, getsegbyname,
# getsectdata, getsectiondata on _NSGetMachExecuteHeader()) or by walking that
# header (CFBundle):
#  - these __TEXT sections: libxpc's launchd/xpcproxy/launchctl identity and
#    config sections, CFBundle's embedded Info.plist, SMJobBless plists;
#  - every section of a segment the toolchain does not make: markers such as
#    __SLSERVER,__slserver (SkyLight's CGSRunningInServer, FuseBoardServices'
#    FURunningInWindowServer), __CGSERVER (AppleGVA, OpenCL), __CGPreLoginApp
#    (SkyLight, AppKit), __RESTRICT (dyld: a restricted process).
# The copies hold no pointers: toolchain segments (__DATA*, __AUTH*) and
# executable segments are never carried. src/process_identity.c applies the
# same rule when the HaoExec route has no stub (keep the two in step).
CARRY = ("__info_plist", "__config", "__launchd", "__launchctl", "__xpcproxy", "__launchd_plist")
TOOLCHAIN_SEGMENTS = ("__PAGEZERO", "__TEXT", "__DATA", "__DATA_CONST", "__DATA_DIRTY", "__AUTH", "__AUTH_CONST",
                      "__LINKEDIT", "__OBJC", "__IMPORT", "__TEXT_EXEC", "__TPRO_CONST")
VM_PROT_EXECUTE = 4
S_ZEROFILL_TYPES = (0x1, 0xC, 0x12)


def arm_slice(data):
    """The arm64 slice hao runs (src/macho.c choose_slice): plain arm64e
    (subtype 2 with any ABI-version bits) > other arm64e.* > arm64; the first
    of equal rank. None if there is no arm64 slice."""
    best, rank = None, 0
    for c, sub, payload in hao_fat.slices(data) or []:
        if c != hao_fat.CPU_ARM64:
            continue
        caps = sub & 0xFF000000
        r = (3 if caps in (0, 0x80000000) else 2) if sub & 0x00FFFFFF == CPU_SUBTYPE_ARM64E else 1
        if r > rank:
            best, rank = payload, r
    return best


def eligible(data, translate=False):
    """None if DATA gets a stub slice, else why not."""
    sl = hao_fat.slices(data)
    if not sl:
        return "not a Mach-O"
    if any(c == hao_fat.CPU_X86_64 for c, _, _ in sl) and not translate:
        return "already has x86_64"
    mo = arm_slice(data)
    if mo is None or len(mo) < 32 or int.from_bytes(mo[12:16], "little") != MH_EXECUTE:
        return "no arm64 executable slice"
    return None if has_lc_main(mo) else "no LC_MAIN (kernel or static image)"


def executable_arm_only(data):
    return eligible(data, False)


# (cmd, offset, cmdsize) of each load command of a thin 64-bit Mach-O. Programs
# come from the image being built, so the walk checks what it reads (ValueError).
load_commands = hao_fat.load_commands


def macho_minos(path):
    """Deployment target 'X.Y[.Z]' of a thin x86_64 Mach-O (object or image)."""
    mo = open(path, "rb").read()
    if int.from_bytes(mo[0:4], "little") != hao_fat.MH_MAGIC_64:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{path}: not a thin 64-bit Mach-O")
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo, path):
        if cmd in (LC_BUILD_VERSION, LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX):
            v = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 12:off + 16] if cmd == LC_BUILD_VERSION else mo[off + 8:off + 12], "little")
            x, y, z = v >> 16, (v >> 8) & 0xFF, v & 0xFF
            return f"{x}.{y}.{z}" if z else f"{x}.{y}"
    raise RuntimeError(f"{path}: no LC_BUILD_VERSION")


def macho_rpaths(path):
    """LC_RPATH entries of a thin x86_64 Mach-O image."""
    mo = open(path, "rb").read()
    if int.from_bytes(mo[0:4], "little") != hao_fat.MH_MAGIC_64:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{path}: not a thin 64-bit Mach-O")
    out = []
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo, path):
        if cmd == 0x8000001C:  # LC_RPATH
            o = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 8:off + 12], "little")
            out.append(mo[off + o:off + size].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace"))
    return out


def sha256_file(path):
    return hashlib.sha256(open(path, "rb").read()).hexdigest()


def build_inputs(stub):
    """The files a relinked stub is made from; each must exist."""
    build = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(stub))
    files = {"front/stub.o": os.path.join(build, "front", "stub.o"), "libhao.dylib": os.path.join(build, "libhao.dylib"),
             "libhao_identity.dylib": os.path.join(build, "libhao_identity.dylib")}
    for name, path in files.items():
        if not os.path.isfile(path):
            raise SystemExit(f"hao-embed: {path} missing: --stub {stub} is not in a complete build directory (run make)")
    return build, files


def has_lc_main(macho):
    try:
        return any(cmd == 0x80000028 for cmd, _, _ in load_commands(macho))   # LC_MAIN
    except ValueError:
        return False


def scan(root):
    """Every arm64-only LC_MAIN executable under ROOT, sorted. Each path of a
    hard-linked program is listed: an image builder can break the link (27.0
    usr/libexec and usr/sbin/appleh13camerad), and launchd may name either."""
    verdict, found = {}, []
    for base, dirs, files in os.walk(root):
        dirs[:] = [d for d in dirs if not os.path.islink(os.path.join(base, d))]
        for name in files:
            path = os.path.join(base, name)
            try:
                st = os.lstat(path)
                if not (st.st_mode & 0o111) or st.st_size < 4096 or not os.path.isfile(path) or os.path.islink(path):
                    continue
                key = (st.st_dev, st.st_ino)
                if key not in verdict:
                    with open(path, "rb") as f:
                        head = f.read(4)
                    verdict[key] = (head in (b"\xcf\xfa\xed\xfe", b"\xca\xfe\xba\xbe", b"\xca\xfe\xba\xbf")
                                    and executable_arm_only(open(path, "rb").read()) is None)
                if verdict[key]:
                    found.append(path)
            except OSError:
                continue
    return sorted(found)


ARCHES = (["--arch", "arm64e"], ["--arch", "arm64"], [])


def identity(path):
    """(identifier, entitlements dict) from the arm64e (else arm64) slice's signature."""
    ident = None
    for arch in ARCHES:
        r = subprocess.run(["codesign", "-d", *arch, "-v", path], capture_output=True, text=True)
        if r.returncode == 0:
            break
    for line in (r.stderr + r.stdout).splitlines():
        if line.startswith("Identifier="):
            ident = line.split("=", 1)[1].strip()
    ents = {}
    for arch in ARCHES:
        r = subprocess.run(["codesign", "-d", *arch, "--entitlements", "-", "--xml", path], capture_output=True)
        if r.returncode == 0:
            break
    blob = r.stdout
    start = blob.find(b"<?xml")
    if start < 0:
        start = blob.find(b"<plist")
    if start >= 0:
        try:
            ents = plistlib.loads(blob[start:])
        except Exception:
            ents = {}
    return ident or os.path.basename(path), ents


def public_only(ents):
    """Host testing: an enforcing AMFI kills ad hoc code claiming restricted
    entitlements, so keep only the public com.apple.security.* set."""
    return {k: v for k, v in ents.items() if k.startswith("com.apple.security.") and ".private." not in k}


def carried(seg, sect, initprot, flags):
    """The CARRY rule for one section of the arm64 executable slice."""
    if seg == "__TEXT":
        return sect in CARRY
    return (seg not in TOOLCHAIN_SEGMENTS and not initprot & VM_PROT_EXECUTE
            and (flags & 0xFF) not in S_ZEROFILL_TYPES)


def carried_sections(data):
    """{(segname, sectname): (bytes, maxprot, initprot)} of the sections the
    stub carries (CARRY) from the arm64 executable slice."""
    out = {}
    for mo in [arm_slice(data)]:
        if mo is None or int.from_bytes(mo[12:16], "little") != MH_EXECUTE:
            continue
        for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
            if cmd != 0x19:
                continue
            seg = mo[off + 8:off + 24].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace")
            maxprot, initprot = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 56:off + 60], "little"), int.from_bytes(mo[off + 60:off + 64], "little")
            nsect = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 64:off + 68], "little")
            if size < 72 or nsect > (size - 72) // 80:
                raise ValueError(f"{seg}: sections overrun the command")
            for k in range(nsect):
                so = off + 72 + 80 * k
                name = mo[so:so + 16].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace")
                flags = int.from_bytes(mo[so + 64:so + 68], "little")
                if not carried(seg, name, initprot, flags):
                    continue
                ssize = int.from_bytes(mo[so + 40:so + 48], "little")
                foff = int.from_bytes(mo[so + 48:so + 52], "little")
                if foff + ssize > len(mo):
                    raise ValueError(f"section {seg},{name} outside the slice")
                out[(seg, name)] = (bytes(mo[foff:foff + ssize]), maxprot, initprot)
        break
    return out


OBJC_LIBS = (b"/usr/lib/libobjc.A.dylib", b"/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreFoundation.framework",
             b"/System/Library/Frameworks/Foundation.framework")


def uses_objc(data):
    """True if the arm64 executable slice links libobjc, CoreFoundation or Foundation."""
    for mo in [arm_slice(data)]:
        if mo is None:
            continue
        for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
            if cmd & 0x7FFFFFFF in (0xC, 0x18, 0x1F, 0x20, 0x23):   # LOAD/WEAK/REEXPORT/LAZY/UPWARD dylib
                name = mo[off + int.from_bytes(mo[off + 8:off + 12], "little"):off + size].split(b"\0")[0]
                if any(name.startswith(p) for p in OBJC_LIBS):
                    return True
        return False
    return True


DYLIB_KINDS = {0xC: "load", 0x80000018: "weak", 0x8000001F: "reexport", 0x20: "lazy", 0x80000023: "upward"}


def dylib_commands(mo):
    """[(kind, install name, current_version, compatibility_version)] of a thin
    Mach-O's dylib load commands, in load-command order (DYLIB_KINDS)."""
    out = []
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd in DYLIB_KINDS:
            if size < 24:
                raise ValueError(f"bad dylib command size {size}")
            no = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 8:off + 12], "little")
            name = mo[off + no:off + size].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace") if 24 <= no < size else ""
            out.append((DYLIB_KINDS[cmd], name, int.from_bytes(mo[off + 16:off + 20], "little"),
                        int.from_bytes(mo[off + 20:off + 24], "little")))
    return out


def macho_uuid(mo):
    """The LC_UUID bytes of a thin Mach-O, or None."""
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd == 0x1B and size >= 24:
            return bytes(mo[off + 8:off + 24])
    return None


# Stubs get their own LC_UUID, a name-based (SHA-1, RFC 4122 version 5) UUID in
# this namespace of the program's arm slice LC_UUID and of the stub's sections,
# so logd, crash reports and everything else keyed by the main executable's
# UUID tell embedded programs apart (a copied hao-stub shares one UUID), and a
# payload stays reproducible. The sections are part of the name because those
# readers take a UUID to name the image's contents: logd keeps one copy of a
# UUID's format strings (/var/db/uuidtext) and resolves a record's format
# offset in it, so two stubs of one program whose strings lie at different
# offsets (another libhao version, other rpaths) under one UUID leave every
# os_log record of the later one as <compose failure>.
STUB_UUID_NAMESPACE = uuid.UUID("6c1f2a4e-9b0d-5e2f-8a51-3d7c0e94b6a1")


def sections_digest(mo):
    """SHA-256 (hex) over every section of the thin Mach-O MO: segment and
    section name, address, size, type and, unless zero-fill, bytes. Signing
    and the load-command edits of apply_identity leave it unchanged."""
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd != 0x19:
            continue
        nsect = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 64:off + 68], "little")
        for k in range(min(nsect, (size - 72) // 80)):
            so = off + 72 + 80 * k
            ssize = int.from_bytes(mo[so + 40:so + 48], "little")
            foff = int.from_bytes(mo[so + 48:so + 52], "little")
            kind = mo[so + 64]
            h.update(bytes(mo[so:so + 48]) + bytes([kind]))   # sectname, segname, addr, size; type
            if kind not in (1, 12, 18):                       # S_ZEROFILL, S_GB_ZEROFILL, S_THREAD_LOCAL_ZEROFILL
                h.update(bytes(mo[foff:foff + ssize]))
    return h.hexdigest()


def stub_uuid(data, stub):
    """The LC_UUID of the stub STUB (a thin x86_64 Mach-O, bytes) of the program DATA (bytes)."""
    mo = arm_slice(data)
    u = macho_uuid(mo) if mo is not None else None
    name = "arm64-uuid:" + uuid.UUID(bytes=u).hex if u else "arm64-sha256:" + hashlib.sha256(mo or data).hexdigest()
    return uuid.uuid5(STUB_UUID_NAMESPACE, name + ";x86_64-sections:" + sections_digest(stub)).bytes


def set_uuid(path, u):
    """Write U into the LC_UUID of the (unsigned) Mach-O at PATH."""
    mo = bytearray(open(path, "rb").read())
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo, path):
        if cmd == 0x1B and size >= 24:
            mo[off + 8:off + 24] = u
            with open(path, "wb") as f:
                f.write(mo)
            return
    raise RuntimeError(f"{path}: no LC_UUID")


PLATFORM_MACOS = 1
PLATFORM_NAMES = {1: "macos", 2: "ios", 3: "tvos", 4: "watchos", 5: "bridgeos", 6: "maccatalyst", 7: "iossimulator",
                  8: "tvossimulator", 9: "watchossimulator", 10: "driverkit", 11: "visionos", 12: "visionossimulator"}


def build_version(mo, what="arm slice"):
    """(platform, minos, sdk) of the image MO as dyld and the kernel read it:
    its one LC_BUILD_VERSION, or LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX (platform macOS).
    RuntimeError for none, or for more than one (a zippered image: dyld
    takes a main executable's platform from one command, and the stub would
    have to choose)."""
    found = []
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo, what):
        if cmd == LC_BUILD_VERSION and size >= 24:
            found.append(struct.unpack_from("<III", mo, off + 8))
        elif cmd == LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX and size >= 16:
            v, sdk = struct.unpack_from("<II", mo, off + 8)
            found.append((PLATFORM_MACOS, v, sdk))
        elif cmd in (0x25, 0x2F, 0x30):  # LC_VERSION_MIN_IPHONEOS, _TVOS, _WATCHOS
            raise RuntimeError(f"{what}: LC_VERSION_MIN for a non-macOS platform (cmd 0x{cmd:x})")
    if len(found) != 1:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{what}: {len(found)} build versions (LC_BUILD_VERSION / LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX); "
                           "the stub carries exactly one")
    return found[0]


def platform_record(mo):
    """The manifest's "platform": [name, minos, sdk] of the image MO."""
    p, minos, sdk = build_version(mo, "stub")
    return [PLATFORM_NAMES.get(p, str(p)), version(minos), version(sdk)]


LC_SOURCE_VERSION, LC_RPATH, LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT, LC_LOAD_DYLINKER, LC_MAIN = 0x2A, 0x8000001C, 0x27, 0xE, 0x80000028
LIBSYSTEM = "/usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib"
SIGNATURE_ROOM = 16   # codesign adds LC_CODE_SIGNATURE in the header padding


def identity_room(mo):
    """Header bytes the stub needs for the arm slice MO's copied load commands."""
    return sum(size for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo) if cmd in identity_rules.COPY) + SIGNATURE_ROOM + 64


def first_section_offset(mo):
    """The lowest file offset of a section with file contents (the end of the header padding)."""
    low = len(mo)
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd == 0x19:
            for k in range(int.from_bytes(mo[off + 64:off + 68], "little")):
                so = off + 72 + 80 * k
                foff, ssize = int.from_bytes(mo[so + 48:so + 52], "little"), int.from_bytes(mo[so + 40:so + 48], "little")
                if foff and ssize and (int.from_bytes(mo[so + 64:so + 68], "little") & 0xFF) not in S_ZEROFILL_TYPES:
                    low = min(low, foff)
    return low


def apply_identity(path, arm, own_rpaths):
    """Give the relinked (unsigned) stub at PATH the arm slice ARM's load-time
    identity by tools/stub_identity_gate.py's RULES: the copied commands
    (LC_BUILD_VERSION whole, with its tools; LC_SOURCE_VERSION; the
    LC_RPATHs, after the stub's own OWN_RPATHS; LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT) and the
    derived fields (LC_MAIN stacksize, the MH flags the kernel reads,
    libSystem's link versions; an LC_VERSION_MIN_MACOSX's minos and sdk in
    the stub's LC_BUILD_VERSION). The load commands are rewritten in the
    header padding (relink_stub reserves identity_room); the file's other
    bytes do not move. RuntimeError if they do not fit or LC_LOAD_DYLINKER
    differs."""
    mo = bytearray(open(path, "rb").read())
    stub_cmds = [(cmd, bytes(mo[off:off + size])) for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo, path)]
    arm_cmds = [(cmd, bytes(arm[off:off + size])) for cmd, off, size in load_commands(arm)]
    of = lambda cmds, kind: [b for c, b in cmds if c == kind]
    if [identity_rules.lc_str(b) for b in of(arm_cmds, LC_LOAD_DYLINKER)] != \
            [identity_rules.lc_str(b) for b in of(stub_cmds, LC_LOAD_DYLINKER)]:
        raise RuntimeError("the arm slice's LC_LOAD_DYLINKER is not the stub's")
    arm_bv, arm_src = of(arm_cmds, LC_BUILD_VERSION), of(arm_cmds, LC_SOURCE_VERSION)
    arm_main = of(arm_cmds, LC_MAIN)
    stub_rpaths = [identity_rules.lc_str(b) for b in of(stub_cmds, LC_RPATH)]
    if stub_rpaths != list(own_rpaths):
        raise RuntimeError(f"the relinked stub's rpaths {stub_rpaths} are not hao-stub's {list(own_rpaths)}")
    extra = [b for b in of(arm_cmds, LC_RPATH) if identity_rules.lc_str(b) not in stub_rpaths]
    extra += of(arm_cmds, LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT)
    arm_libsystem = [(cur, compat) for kind, name, cur, compat in dylib_commands(arm) if name == LIBSYSTEM]
    out, inserted = [], False
    last_rpath = max([k for k, (c, _) in enumerate(stub_cmds) if c == LC_RPATH], default=None)
    for k, (cmd, b) in enumerate(stub_cmds):
        if cmd == LC_BUILD_VERSION:
            if arm_bv:
                b = arm_bv[0]
            else:
                b = bytearray(b)
                struct.pack_into("<III", b, 8, *build_version(arm))
                b = bytes(b)
        elif cmd == LC_SOURCE_VERSION:
            if not arm_src:
                continue
            b = arm_src[0]
        elif cmd == LC_MAIN and arm_main:
            b = bytearray(b)
            b[16:24] = arm_main[0][16:24]
            b = bytes(b)
        elif cmd in (0xC, 0x80000018) and arm_libsystem and identity_rules.lc_str(b) == LIBSYSTEM:
            b = bytearray(b)
            struct.pack_into("<II", b, 16, *arm_libsystem[0])
            b = bytes(b)
        out.append(b)
        if k == last_rpath:
            out += extra
            inserted = True
    if not inserted:
        out += extra
    if arm_src and not of(stub_cmds, LC_SOURCE_VERSION):
        out += arm_src
    blob = b"".join(out)
    if 32 + len(blob) + SIGNATURE_ROOM > first_section_offset(mo):
        raise RuntimeError(f"no room for the program's load commands ({len(blob)} bytes) in the stub's header")
    old = int.from_bytes(mo[20:24], "little")
    mo[32:32 + max(old, len(blob))] = blob + bytes(max(0, old - len(blob)))
    struct.pack_into("<II", mo, 16, len(out), len(blob))
    flags = int.from_bytes(mo[24:28], "little") & ~identity_rules.MH_POLICY_FLAGS
    flags |= int.from_bytes(arm[24:28], "little") & identity_rules.MH_POLICY_FLAGS
    struct.pack_into("<I", mo, 24, flags)
    with open(path, "wb") as f:
        f.write(mo)


def pagezero_size(mo):
    """__PAGEZERO's vmsize in the arm slice MO (the kernel reserves it); RuntimeError if it has none."""
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd == 0x19 and mo[off + 8:off + 24].split(b"\0")[0] == b"__PAGEZERO":
            return int.from_bytes(mo[off + 32:off + 40], "little")
    raise RuntimeError("the arm slice has no __PAGEZERO")


HOST_X86_CACHES = ("/System/Volumes/Preboot/Cryptexes/Rosetta/System/Library/dyld",
                   "/System/Volumes/Preboot/Cryptexes/OS/System/Library/dyld", "/System/Library/dyld")
ROOT_X86_CACHES = ("System/Library/dyld", "System/Cryptexes/OS/System/Library/dyld",
                   "System/Volumes/Preboot/Cryptexes/Rosetta/System/Library/dyld")
X86_CACHE_FILE = "dyld_shared_cache_x86_64"
LIBCXX = "/usr/lib/libc++.1.dylib"
CF_PATH = "/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreFoundation.framework/Versions/A/CoreFoundation"


class X86Libraries:
    """The libraries a stub can load natively at launch, as src/runtime.c binds a
    dependency (try_candidate: native dlopen first, then a guest image): an
    install name or path of the system's x86_64 shared cache, or a file under
    ROOT with an x86_64 slice. Everything else (arm64-only files, the arm64e
    cache's own libraries) loads as a guest image and is not linked."""

    def __init__(self, cache_dir, root="/"):
        import hao_macho       # shared format reader
        self.bc = hao_macho
        self.root = os.path.abspath(root)
        self.cache_dir = cache_dir
        self.cache = hao_macho.Cache(os.path.join(cache_dir, X86_CACHE_FILE))
        self.ids = self.cache.ids()
        self.uuid = self.cache.uuid
        self._disk = {}

    def _file(self, path):
        """'x86', 'arm' or None for the file at PATH (a real path under ROOT)."""
        if path not in self._disk:
            sl = self.bc.file_slices(path) if os.path.isfile(path) else []
            self._disk[path] = ("x86" if any(c == self.bc.CPU_X86_64 for c, _, _ in sl) else
                                "arm" if any(c == self.bc.CPU_ARM64 for c, _, _ in sl) else None)
        return self._disk[path]

    def under_root(self, p):
        return os.path.normpath(os.path.join(self.root, p.lstrip("/"))) if p.startswith("/") else p

    def os_path(self, f):
        """The path on the running system of F (a normalised path under ROOT), or None."""
        if self.root == "/":
            return f
        return f[len(self.root):] if f.startswith(self.root + "/") else None

    def candidates(self, name, exe, rpaths):
        """The files under ROOT dyld tries for NAME as a dependency of the main
        executable EXE (a real path under ROOT), in order."""
        d = os.path.dirname(exe)
        if name.startswith("@executable_path/") or name.startswith("@loader_path/"):
            return [os.path.normpath(d + name[name.index("/"):])]
        if name.startswith("@rpath/"):
            out = []
            for rp in rpaths:
                if rp.startswith("@executable_path") or rp.startswith("@loader_path"):
                    base = d + rp[rp.index("_path") + 5:]
                elif rp.startswith("/"):
                    base = self.under_root(rp)
                else:
                    continue
                out.append(os.path.normpath(base + "/" + name[7:]))
            return out
        return [self.under_root(name)] if name.startswith("/") else []

    def resolve(self, name, exe, rpaths):
        """('cache', OS path) | ('disk', file) | ('guest', file) | (None, None) for NAME."""
        for f in self.candidates(name, exe, rpaths):
            op = self.os_path(f)
            if op is not None and op in self.ids:
                return "cache", op
            kind = self._file(f)
            if kind == "x86":
                return "disk", f
            if kind == "arm":
                return "guest", f
        return None, None

    def closure(self, names):
        """Cache paths of the images that loading the cache images NAMES
        brings in (non-lazy dependencies, transitively), NAMES included."""
        seen, todo = set(), [n for n in names if n in self.ids]
        while todo:
            n = todo.pop()
            p = self.ids.get(n, n)
            if p in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(p)
            im = self.cache.image(p)
            for kind, dep in (im.deps if im else []):
                if kind != "lazy" and dep in self.ids:
                    todo.append(dep)
        return seen


def native_deps(path, data, x86, stub_deps=()):
    """The program's dependencies the stub links, and the ones it does not:
    (links, skipped, rpaths) with links [(kind, name, current, compat)] in the
    program's load-command order (weak stays weak; re-export and upward are
    plain loads), skipped [(name, why)], and rpaths the program's LC_RPATHs
    when a linked dependency is an @rpath name (else []). A dependency is linked
    when it resolves natively (X86Libraries.resolve). Not linked: libraries the
    stub links itself (STUB_DEPS), lazy loads (not loaded at launch natively
    either), libraries that load as guest images or are missing, and a file
    with an arm64 slice the program imports C++ names from (src/runtime.c
    guest_cxx_library may run it as guest code, but not once it is loaded)."""
    mo = arm_slice(data)
    exe = os.path.realpath(path)
    rpaths = macho_rpaths_mo(mo)
    deps = dylib_commands(mo)
    cxx = cxx_ordinals(path, mo)
    links, skipped, need_rpaths = [], [], False
    for k, (kind, name, cur, compat) in enumerate(deps):
        if name in stub_deps:
            continue
        if kind == "lazy":
            skipped.append((name, "lazy"))
            continue
        where, f = x86.resolve(name, exe, rpaths)
        if where is None:
            skipped.append((name, "not found"))
            continue
        if where == "guest":
            skipped.append((name, "guest image"))
            continue
        if where == "disk" and k + 1 in cxx and x86._file(f) == "x86" and has_arm_slice(f) and name != LIBCXX:
            skipped.append((name, "C++ interface with an arm64 slice (guest_cxx_library)"))
            continue
        links.append(("weak" if kind == "weak" else "load", name, cur, compat))
        need_rpaths |= name.startswith("@rpath/")
    return links, skipped, rpaths if need_rpaths else []


def has_arm_slice(path):
    return any(c == hao_fat.CPU_ARM64 for c, _, _ in (hao_fat.slices(open(path, "rb").read()) or []))


def macho_rpaths_mo(mo):
    out = []
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd == 0x8000001C:  # LC_RPATH
            o = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 8:off + 12], "little")
            out.append(mo[off + o:off + size].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace"))
    return out


def cxx_ordinals(path, mo):
    """Library ordinals the program imports a C++ (__Z) name from (src/macho.c dep_cxx)."""
    import hao_macho
    try:
        imports = hao_macho.Image(lambda o, n: mo[o:o + n], 0, path).imports()
    except (ValueError, IndexError, struct.error):
        return set()
    return {o for o, name, _ in imports if o > 0 and name.startswith("__Z")}


def version(v):
    return "%d.%d.%d" % (v >> 16, (v >> 8) & 0xFF, v & 0xFF)


def tbd_for(path, name, cur, compat):
    """An install-name-only text stub: linking against it records NAME (with
    the program's own versions) and nothing else (no symbols)."""
    q = name.replace("'", "''")
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write("--- !tapi-tbd\ntbd-version: 4\ntargets: [ x86_64-macos ]\n"
                f"install-name: '{q}'\ncurrent-version: {version(cur)}\ncompatibility-version: {version(compat)}\n...\n")


# Skeletons: ld's output for one program with every -sectcreate section and LC_UUID zeroed, so that it
# holds no bytes of the program (the carried sections are the program's; the rest is hao's stub.o,
# libhao, install names and sizes). --save-skeletons writes one per relinked stub, keyed by the
# program file's sha256; --skeletons fills them from the program instead of running ld, which gives the
# same bytes, so a Mac without Apple's ld for the stub's deployment target can still embed.
SKELETONS = {"save": None, "use": None}


def skeleton_key(data):
    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()


def section_ranges(mo, wanted):
    """{(segname, sectname): (fileoff, size)} of WANTED's sections in the thin Mach-O MO."""
    out = {}
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd != 0x19:
            continue
        seg = mo[off + 8:off + 24].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace")
        nsect = int.from_bytes(mo[off + 64:off + 68], "little")
        for k in range(nsect):
            so = off + 72 + 80 * k
            name = mo[so:so + 16].split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace")
            if (seg, name) in wanted:
                out[(seg, name)] = (int.from_bytes(mo[so + 48:so + 52], "little"),
                                    int.from_bytes(mo[so + 40:so + 48], "little"))
    return out


def save_skeleton(linked, sections, key):
    mo = bytearray(open(linked, "rb").read())
    ranges = section_ranges(mo, set(sections))
    if set(ranges) != set(sections):
        raise RuntimeError("skeleton: sections missing from the link")
    for (seg, name), (off, size) in ranges.items():
        if size != len(sections[(seg, name)][0]) or off + size > len(mo):
            raise RuntimeError(f"skeleton: section {seg},{name} is not the carried bytes")
        mo[off:off + size] = bytes(size)
    for cmd, off, size in load_commands(mo):
        if cmd == 0x1B and size >= 24:
            mo[off + 8:off + 24] = bytes(16)
    d = SKELETONS["save"]
    with open(os.path.join(d, key + ".skel"), "wb") as f:
        f.write(mo)
    with open(os.path.join(d, key + ".json"), "w") as f:
        json.dump({"sections": sorted([seg, name, off, size] for (seg, name), (off, size) in ranges.items())},
                  f, sort_keys=True)


def fill_skeleton(sections, key, out):
    d = SKELETONS["use"]
    path = os.path.join(d, key + ".skel")
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        raise RuntimeError("no skeleton " + key)
    mo = bytearray(open(path, "rb").read())
    meta = json.load(open(os.path.join(d, key + ".json")))["sections"]
    if {(seg, name) for seg, name, _, _ in meta} != set(sections):
        raise RuntimeError("skeleton " + key + ": its sections are not this program's")
    for seg, name, off, size in meta:
        blob = sections[(seg, name)][0]
        if len(blob) != size or off + size > len(mo) or any(mo[off:off + size]):
            raise RuntimeError(f"skeleton {key}: section {seg},{name} does not fit")
        mo[off:off + size] = blob
    with open(out, "wb") as f:
        f.write(mo)
    return out


def relink_stub(sections, work, build, stub, host_test=False, links=(), uuid_of=None, arm=None, key=None):
    """hao-stub linked again with the program's carried sections (unsigned),
    from BUILD/front/stub.o at that object's own deployment target, with the
    rpaths STUB (the Makefile's hao-stub) was linked with; LINKS (native_deps)
    are linked after libhao and libhao_identity, in order, through
    install-name-only text stubs (libSystem, which the stub needs for its own
    code, at its place in the order). With UUID_OF (the program) its LC_UUID
    becomes stub_uuid's; with
    ARM (the program's arm slice) the stub gets that slice's __PAGEZERO size
    and then its load-time identity (apply_identity)."""
    obj = os.path.join(build, "front", "stub.o")
    args = ["clang", "-arch", "x86_64", "-mmacosx-version-min=" + macho_minos(obj), obj, "-L" + build, "-lhao", "-lhao_identity"]
    for k, (kind, name, cur, compat) in enumerate(links):
        if name == LIBSYSTEM and kind == "load":
            args.append("-lSystem")   # the SDK's: the stub's code binds to it (apply_identity sets the versions)
            continue
        t = os.path.join(work, "dep%d.tbd" % k)
        tbd_for(t, name, cur, compat)
        args += ["-Wl,-weak_library," + t] if kind == "weak" else [t]
    own_rpaths = [r for r in macho_rpaths(stub) if r != build] + ([build] if host_test else [])
    args += ["-Wl,-no_adhoc_codesign"] + ["-Wl,-rpath," + r for r in own_rpaths]
    if arm is not None:
        args += ["-Wl,-headerpad,0x%x" % identity_room(arm), "-Wl,-pagezero_size,0x%x" % pagezero_size(arm)]
    prots = {}
    for k, ((seg, name), (blob, maxprot, initprot)) in enumerate(sorted(sections.items())):
        path = os.path.join(work, "sect%d" % k)
        with open(path, "wb") as f:
            f.write(blob)
        args += ["-Wl,-sectcreate,%s,%s,%s" % (seg, name, path)]
        if seg != "__TEXT":
            prots[seg] = (maxprot, initprot)
    letters = lambda p: "".join(c for b, c in ((1, "r"), (2, "w"), (4, "x")) if p & b) or "-"
    for seg, (maxprot, initprot) in sorted(prots.items()):
        args += ["-Wl,-segprot,%s,%s,%s" % (seg, letters(maxprot), letters(initprot))]
    out = os.path.join(work, "stub-relinked")
    if key is not None and SKELETONS["use"]:
        fill_skeleton(sections, key, out)
    else:
        r = subprocess.run(args + ["-o", out], capture_output=True, text=True)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            raise RuntimeError("relink: " + r.stderr.strip()[-300:])
        if key is not None and SKELETONS["save"]:
            save_skeleton(out, sections, key)
    if uuid_of is not None:
        set_uuid(out, stub_uuid(uuid_of, open(out, "rb").read()))
    if arm is not None:
        apply_identity(out, arm, own_rpaths)
    return out


SLICE_SECTION = ("__TEXT", "__hao_slice")
SLICE_MAGIC = b"haoslice"


def slice_record(arm):
    """The stub's __TEXT,__hao_slice for the arm slice ARM (include/hao/macho.h
    hao_slice_record): magic, version 1, the CodeDirectory's hash type, two
    zero bytes and its cdhash. RuntimeError if the slice's signature is
    missing or would not verify under hao."""
    try:
        c = hao_codesig.check(bytes(arm))
    except ValueError as e:
        raise RuntimeError(f"the arm slice's load commands: {e}")
    if c["verdict"] == "unsigned":
        raise RuntimeError("the arm slice is not code signed (hao runs an embedded program only from signed code)")
    if c["verdict"] != "valid":
        raise RuntimeError(f"the arm slice's code signature is not valid ({c['why']})")
    return SLICE_MAGIC + bytes([1, c["hash_type"], 0, 0]) + c["cdhash"]


def hardened(data):
    """True if the program's own signature makes dyld ignore DYLD_* variables (tools/hao_codesig.py)."""
    if data is None:
        return False
    return hao_codesig.dyld_env_blocked(hao_codesig.info(arm_slice(data) or b""))


BOUND_SLOTS = ((hao_codesig.CSSLOT_INFOSLOT, "Info.plist"), (hao_codesig.CSSLOT_RESOURCEDIR, "_CodeSignature/CodeResources"))
INFO_SECTION = ("__TEXT", "__info_plist")


def bundle_contents(path):
    """The Contents directory of the bundle whose Contents/MacOS holds PATH, else None."""
    d = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(path))
    if os.path.basename(d) == "MacOS" and os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(d)) == "Contents":
        return os.path.dirname(d)
    return None


def bound_data(path, data):
    """[(slot, source, bytes)] for special slots -1 (Info.plist) and -3
    (resource seal) as the arm slice's signature binds them: source is the
    bundle file whose bytes have the arm slice's slot hash (Contents/Info.plist,
    Contents/_CodeSignature/CodeResources), or for slot -1 the carried
    __TEXT,__info_plist section of a tool; (slot, None, None) where the arm
    slice binds nothing. RuntimeError if the arm slice binds data that neither
    matches (the bundle on disk differs from its signature)."""
    mo = arm_slice(data)
    contents = bundle_contents(path)
    section = carried_sections(data).get(INFO_SECTION)
    out = []
    for slot, name in BOUND_SLOTS:
        want = hao_codesig.special_slots(mo, slot)
        if not want:
            out.append((slot, None, None))
            continue
        cands = []
        if contents and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(contents, name)):
            f = os.path.join(contents, name)
            cands.append((f, open(f, "rb").read()))
        if slot == hao_codesig.CSSLOT_INFOSLOT and section:
            cands.append((",".join(INFO_SECTION), section[0]))
        for src, blob in cands:
            if all(hao_codesig.digest(t, blob) == h for t, h in want.items()):
                out.append((slot, src, blob))
                break
        else:
            raise RuntimeError(f"signature binds a {name} (slot -{slot}) that " +
                               (f"{', '.join(c for c, _ in cands)} does not match" if cands else "is not found"))
    return out


def cs_copied_flags(mo):
    """codesign -o names of the arm slice MO's CodeDirectory flags the stub copies."""
    if mo is None:
        return []
    _, flags = identity_rules.cd_fields(mo)
    return [nm for bit, nm in sorted(identity_rules.CS_COPIED_FLAGS.items()) if flags & bit]


def signed_stub(src, stub, work, host_test, data=None, x86=None):
    """Sign a copy of the stub as SRC's identity; returns (path, identifier,
    entitlement keys, bound, deps) with bound from bound_data (the slots set)
    and deps (links, skipped) from native_deps. With DATA the stub is always
    relinked: it links the program's native dependencies (X86, an
    X86Libraries), gets its own LC_UUID (stub_uuid) and the arm slice's
    load-time identity (apply_identity; a load command no rule names is
    refused, tools/stub_identity_gate.py RULES)."""
    sections = carried_sections(data) if data is not None else {}
    links, skipped = [], []
    if data is not None and not uses_objc(data):
        sections[("__TEXT", "__hao_noreexec")] = (b"\1", 5, 5)
    arm = arm_slice(data) if data is not None else None
    if data is not None:
        identity_rules.check_rules(arm)
        build_version(arm)   # exactly one (a zippered program is refused)
        sections[SLICE_SECTION] = (slice_record(arm), 5, 5)
        own = {name for _, name, _, _ in dylib_commands(open(stub, "rb").read())} - {LIBSYSTEM}
        links, skipped, _ = native_deps(src, data, x86, own)
        stub = relink_stub(sections, work, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(stub)), stub, host_test,
                           links, data, arm, skeleton_key(data))
    elif sections or host_test:
        stub = relink_stub(sections, work, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(stub)), stub, host_test)
    ident, ents = identity(src)
    ents = public_only(ents) if host_test else dict(ents)
    ents.update(JIT_ENTITLEMENTS)
    entfile = os.path.join(work, "ents.plist")
    with open(entfile, "wb") as f:
        plistlib.dump(ents, f)
    copy = os.path.join(work, "stub")
    shutil.copyfile(stub, copy)
    os.chmod(copy, 0o755)
    # dyld ignores DYLD_* variables for the program natively (platform or
    # hardened runtime): the stub gets the hardened runtime, which does the
    # same for it. Otherwise an injected library would run with the
    # program's entitlements and identity before libhao.
    # The kernel's treatment of invalid pages (CS_KILL, CS_HARD, CS_ENFORCEMENT)
    # is the program's (tools/stub_identity_gate.py CS_COPIED_FLAGS).
    opts = (["runtime"] if hardened(data) else []) + cs_copied_flags(arm)
    r = subprocess.run(["codesign", "-s", "-", "-f", "-i", ident] + (["-o", ",".join(opts)] if opts else []) +
                       ["--entitlements", entfile, copy], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError("codesign: " + r.stderr.strip())
    bound = bound_data(src, data) if data is not None else []
    if bound:
        signed = hao_codesig.bind_special_slots(open(copy, "rb").read(), {slot: blob for slot, _, blob in bound})
        with open(copy, "wb") as f:
            f.write(signed)
    return copy, ident, sorted(ents), [(slot, s, b) for slot, s, b in bound if s], (links, skipped)


def x86_cache_dir(a):
    """--x86-cache, else (--stubs) the x86_64 cache under --root, else this host's."""
    cands = [a.x86_cache] if a.x86_cache else \
        [os.path.join(a.root, d) for d in ROOT_X86_CACHES] if a.stubs else list(HOST_X86_CACHES)
    for d in cands:
        if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, X86_CACHE_FILE)):
            return d
    sys.exit(f"hao-embed: no {X86_CACHE_FILE} in {', '.join(cands)}" +
             ("" if a.x86_cache else " (give --x86-cache DIR: the release's RosettaOS or OS cryptex dyld directory)"))


def write_like(dst, data, like, in_place=False):
    """Write DATA to DST with LIKE's owner and mode. In place (DST is LIKE)
    the inode is kept, so other hard links see the embedded file too; a
    symlink is refused rather than replaced by a copy."""
    if in_place and os.path.islink(dst):
        raise RuntimeError("is a symlink; embed the file it names")
    st = os.stat(like)
    if in_place:
        with open(dst, "r+b") as f:
            f.write(data)
            f.truncate()
            f.flush()
            os.fsync(f.fileno())
        return
    tmp = dst + ".hao-embed"
    with open(tmp, "wb") as f:
        f.write(data)
    if os.geteuid() == 0:
        os.chown(tmp, st.st_uid, st.st_gid)
    os.chmod(tmp, st.st_mode & 0o7777)
    os.rename(tmp, dst)


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("--stub", default=DEFAULT_STUB)
    ap.add_argument("--host-test", action="store_true",
                    help="keep only public entitlements and add an rpath to the stub's build directory "
                         "(for running on an AMFI-enforcing development host)")
    ap.add_argument("--translate", action="store_true",
                    help="also give universal programs the stub, in place of their own x86_64 slices")
    if len(sys.argv) == 3 and sys.argv[1] == "--scan":
        print("\n".join(scan(sys.argv[2])))
        return 0
    g = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    g.add_argument("--in-place", action="store_true")
    g.add_argument("-o", "--out", help="output file (one PROGRAM) or directory")
    g.add_argument("--stubs", help="write signed stubs and manifest.json here")
    ap.add_argument("--root", help="with --stubs: image root the manifest paths are relative to")
    ap.add_argument("--list", help="file with one PROGRAM per line")
    ap.add_argument("--scan", action="store_true", help="with --stubs: embed every arm64-only program under --root")
    ap.add_argument("--require", action="append", default=[], metavar="REL",
                    help="with --stubs: hao-install.py fails unless REL (relative to --root) is embedded")
    ap.add_argument("--require-embedded", action="store_true",
                    help="with --stubs: every manifest entry is required")
    ap.add_argument("--x86-cache", metavar="DIR",
                    help="directory of the dyld_shared_cache_x86_64 the stubs run with (default: with --stubs, "
                         "the one under --root; otherwise this host's)")
    sk = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    sk.add_argument("--save-skeletons", metavar="DIR",
                    help="also write each relinked stub's skeleton (its program's bytes zeroed) to DIR")
    sk.add_argument("--skeletons", metavar="DIR",
                    help="fill the skeletons in DIR from each program instead of running ld")
    ap.add_argument("programs", nargs="*")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    if a.save_skeletons:
        os.makedirs(a.save_skeletons, exist_ok=True)
    SKELETONS["save"], SKELETONS["use"] = a.save_skeletons, a.skeletons
    if not os.path.exists(a.stub):
        sys.exit(f"hao-embed: no stub at {a.stub} (run make)")
    if a.scan and not a.root:
        sys.exit("hao-embed: --scan needs --root")
    _, inputs = build_inputs(a.stub)
    progs = list(a.programs)
    if a.list:
        progs += [l.strip() for l in open(a.list) if l.strip()]
    if a.scan:
        progs += scan(a.root)
    if (a.require or a.require_embedded) and not a.stubs:
        sys.exit("hao-embed: --require and --require-embedded need --stubs")
    if a.stubs:
        if not a.root:
            sys.exit("hao-embed: --stubs needs --root")
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(a.stubs, "stubs"), exist_ok=True)
    x86 = X86Libraries(x86_cache_dir(a), a.root if a.stubs else "/") if progs else None
    manifest, bad, seen = [], 0, {}
    for p in progs:
        # A path listed twice, or a symlink to a program already listed, is one program.
        if a.in_place and os.path.islink(p):
            print(f"fail\t{p}\tis a symlink; embed the file it names")
            bad += 1
            continue
        real = os.path.realpath(p)
        if real in seen:
            print(f"skip\t{p}\tsame file as {seen[real]}")
            continue
        seen[real] = p
        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="hao-embed.") as work:
            try:
                data = open(p, "rb").read()
                why = eligible(data, a.translate)
                if why:
                    print(f"skip\t{p}\t{why}")
                    continue
                translate = hao_fat.has_cpu(data, hao_fat.CPU_X86_64)
                stub, ident, keys, bound, (links, skipped) = signed_stub(p, a.stub, work, a.host_test, data, x86)
                stub_bytes = open(stub, "rb").read()
                merged = hao_fat.combine(data, stub_bytes, drop_x86_64=translate)
                if a.stubs:
                    rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.realpath(p), os.path.realpath(a.root))
                    if rel.startswith(".."):
                        raise RuntimeError(f"not under {a.root}")
                    name = hashlib.sha256(rel.encode()).hexdigest()[:24] + ".stub"
                    with open(os.path.join(a.stubs, "stubs", name), "wb") as f:
                        f.write(stub_bytes)
                    entry = {"path": rel, "identifier": ident, "stub": "stubs/" + name,
                             "stub_sha256": hashlib.sha256(stub_bytes).hexdigest(),
                             "source_sha256": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(),
                             "result_sha256": hashlib.sha256(merged).hexdigest(),
                             "entitlements": keys, "bound": [],
                             "uuid": str(uuid.UUID(bytes=macho_uuid(stub_bytes))).upper(),
                             "platform": platform_record(stub_bytes),
                             "links": len(links), "weak_links": sum(k == "weak" for k, _, _, _ in links),
                             "not_linked": [[n, why] for n, why in skipped],
                             "corefoundation": CF_PATH in x86.closure([n for _, n, _, _ in links])}
                    for slot, bsrc, blob in bound:
                        b = {"slot": -slot, "sha256": hashlib.sha256(blob).hexdigest()}
                        if bsrc == ",".join(INFO_SECTION):
                            b["section"] = bsrc
                        else:
                            b["file"] = os.path.relpath(bsrc, os.path.realpath(a.root))
                            if b["file"].startswith(".."):
                                raise RuntimeError(f"{bsrc} is not under {a.root}")
                        entry["bound"].append(b)
                    if translate:
                        entry["mode"] = "translate"
                    manifest.append(entry)
                else:
                    if a.in_place:
                        dst = p
                    elif os.path.isdir(a.out):
                        dst = os.path.join(a.out, os.path.basename(p))
                    else:
                        dst = a.out
                    write_like(dst, merged, p, in_place=a.in_place)
                print(f"{'translated' if translate else 'ok'}\t{p}\t{ident}\tlinks {len(links)}" +
                      (f" (not {len(skipped)})" if skipped else "") +
                      "".join(f"\tbound -{slot} {os.path.basename(bsrc)}" for slot, bsrc, _ in bound))
            except (OSError, RuntimeError, ValueError) as e:
                print(f"fail\t{p}\t{e}")
                bad += 1
    if a.stubs:
        required = a.require + ([e["path"] for e in manifest] if a.require_embedded else [])
        required = list(dict.fromkeys(required))
        with open(os.path.join(a.stubs, "manifest.json"), "w") as f:
            json.dump({"stub_sha256": sha256_file(a.stub), "x86_cache_uuid": x86.uuid if x86 else None,
                       "inputs_sha256": {k: sha256_file(v) for k, v in inputs.items()},
                       "required": required, "files": manifest}, f, indent=1)
            f.write("\n")
    return 1 if bad else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
